WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.148
The only thing this chapter ever
writes is the two agent policies,

2
00:00:04.148 --> 00:00:06.500
report-only, and that's the kit's design.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.714
The plan compares the two reviewed
policies with the tenant's,

4
00:00:10.714 --> 00:00:13.688
and says create, in place,
or differs for each.

5
00:00:13.688 --> 00:00:18.115
Where decision D N six says agent
Conditional Access isn't published,

6
00:00:18.115 --> 00:00:19.901
it marks them not available.

7
00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:23.663
And it refuses a reviewed file
that isn't report-only Block.

8
00:00:23.663 --> 00:00:25.888
The write path is a separate script.

9
00:00:25.888 --> 00:00:29.902
It refuses to run unless the
plan's hash is the approved one,

10
00:00:29.902 --> 00:00:33.749
for this tenant and cloud, and
no more than seven days old.

11
00:00:33.749 --> 00:00:38.375
Every write creates a report-only
policy with Block as the only grant.

12
00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:42.388
It runs as a person with the
Conditional Access Administrator role.

13
00:00:42.388 --> 00:00:44.326
And it never turns a policy on.

14
00:00:44.326 --> 00:00:49.168
Microsoft Learn's page on Conditional
Access for agents lists the feature as

15
00:00:49.168 --> 00:00:54.290
preview, so that waits until the agent
targets leave preview in the agency's cloud.
